---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const updated = "11 July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="TableRead — Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for TableRead, the native Mac casting and AI table-read app by DataIsland Software LLC, part of the PolySpeak suite."
>

  <section class="legal fade-in">
    <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/privacy">← All Privacy Policies</a></div>

    <h1>TableRead — Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">DataIsland Software LLC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <p>
      TableRead is a native Mac casting and AI table-read app, part of the PolySpeak
      voice-production suite. This policy explains exactly what data TableRead accesses
      and — importantly — confirms that nothing it processes ever leaves your device.
    </p>

    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>TableRead makes no network requests of any kind.</strong> Casting, script
      reading, and AI table-read generation all run entirely on your Mac using a local
      voice pipeline. There is no cloud AI feature in TableRead — unlike PolyScript's
      optional AI tab, TableRead's read-through generation never touches the network.
      The app has no server, no account, and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What TableRead Accesses</h2>
    <p>TableRead accesses only data on your Mac that's needed to cast and read your script:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Script files you explicitly open (.fountain, .fusiondoc)</li>
      <li>A shared local voice-library folder, read to populate the casting picker with available voice models</li>
      <li>A nearby <code>.polyproject</code> manifest file, if one exists near the open script, which TableRead may write progress information into</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      TableRead does not access your microphone — it doesn't record audio, only generates
      read-throughs from text using existing voice models. It also does not access your
      camera, contacts, location, photos, or calendar.
    </p>

    <h2>What Leaves Your Device</h2>

    <h3>Nothing, Ever</h3>
    <p>
      This is worth stating plainly: TableRead's AI read-through generation runs a local
      Python/RVC voice pipeline entirely on your Mac via a subprocess. No script text,
      dialogue, casting choice, or generated audio is ever uploaded anywhere. There is no
      cloud AI feature in TableRead at all — the entire pipeline, from script to finished
      read-through, executes on-device with no network connection involved.
    </p>

    <h2>What Is Stored Locally</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Script files</strong> — wherever you saved them</li>
      <li><strong>Generated read-through audio files</strong> — saved to locations you choose on your Mac</li>
      <li><strong>The shared voice library</strong> — local voice models used for casting</li>
      <li><strong>Casting assignments</strong> — saved back into the script's own file</li>
    </ul>
    <p>None of this data is synced to iCloud or transmitted to DataIsland.</p>

    <h2>What TableRead Does Not Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Does not transmit any data anywhere — script text, casting, and generated audio all stay on your Mac</li>
      <li>Does not require an account or login</li>
      <li>Does not collect analytics, usage statistics, or crash reports</li>
      <li>Does not access your files without your explicit action</li>
      <li>Does not access your microphone</li>
      <li>Does not share data with third parties</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      TableRead is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
      information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we make material changes to this policy, we will update the "Last updated" date above.
      Continued use of TableRead after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy:<br />
      <a href="mailto:support@dataisland.com">support@dataisland.com</a><br />
      DataIsland Software LLC
    </p>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .breadcrumb { margin-bottom: 2rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }

  .legal h1 { font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .meta { font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--gray); margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  .legal h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-size: 1.2rem; }
  .legal h3 { margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .legal p  { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }

  ul {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--gray-dark);
  }

  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.4rem; font-size: 0.97rem; line-height: 1.5; }
</style>
